    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0512" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg416"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore to Mr. Draper.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Draper</hi>:</p>
                <p>I have acknowledged officially to-day, to Mr. Iddings, your dispatch No. 237, of
                    June 22 last, touching the desire of the Italian Government that the order of
                    May 27 last, to the United States consul at Naples, in reference to emigrant
                    inspections be extended to our consulates at Genoa and Palermo, and have told
                    him that the consul general at Rome was instructed by telegraph, on the 27th
                    ultimo, to go to Naples and investigate the matter of the inspection of
                    emigrants. This telegram has been followed by an instruction by mail directing
                    the consul general to visit also the other consulates in Italy and to make an
                    investigation of the inspection of emigrants at those points as well as a
                    general investigation of the consulates.</p>
                <p>I advise you of this, knowing your interest in the matter.</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore.</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
